ociated with skin and respiratory flora and poses a particular risk to individuals with compromised health. This bacterium is known for its ability to cause a range of infections, highlighting its significance in both clinical and community settings.", "ENTEROCOCO:Enterococcus, also referred to as Enterococo, is a genus of bacteria that is commonly found as part of the normal intestinal flora. However, it has the potential to cause infections, particularly in patients with weakened immune systems or those with central venous catheters (CVC). These infections can be serious and are more likely to occur in individuals who are already vulnerable due to underlying health conditions.", "PSEUDOMONAS:Pseudomonas is a genus of bacteria that can cause infections, particularly in immunocompromised patients.", "CANDIDA SPP.:Candida species are fungi that can cause infections, especially in patients with prolonged neutropenia or those undergoing certain treatments.", "DETECCIÓN DE TROMBOSIS VENOSA:Detection of venous thrombosis involves various diagnostic procedures to confirm the presence of thrombus in the venous system.", "NO DETECCIÓN DE TROMBOSIS VENOSA:No detection of venous thrombosis indicates that despite clinical suspicion, no thrombus was found.", "VALORAR ESTUDIO TROMBOFILIA:Evaluating thrombophilia involves assessing selected cases for underlying conditions that predispose individuals to thrombosis.", "MONITORIZACIÓN:Monitoring refers to the ongoing assessment of patients, particularly those undergoing treatment for thrombosis, to ensure effective management and detect complications.", "TROMBOSIS SÉPTICA:Septic thrombosis refers to the presence of a thrombus associated with a systemic infection, leading to complications.", "ENDOCARDITIS:Endocarditis is an infection of the inner lining of the heart, often considered a serious complication that can arise from catheter-related infections. It is particularly associated with patients who have central venous catheters (CVC). This condition poses significant health risks and requires careful management to prevent severe outcomes.", "METÁSTASIS A DISTANCIA:Distant metastasis refers to the spread of cancer cells from the original tumor site to other parts of the body, which can complicate treatment in patients with CVC.", "GÉRMENES GRAM POSITIVOS:Gram-positive germs are a category of bacteria that are frequently involved in infections, particularly in patients with CVC.", "BACILOS GRAM NEGATIVOS:Gram-negative bacilli are a type of bacteria that can cause infections, especially in patients with compromised immune systems."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}